e designed to demonstrate the practical application of informed and uninformed search algorithms within an interactive web-based environment. Developed using Python, Flask, HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, the project centers on a classic word chain puzzle where each new word must start with the last letter of the previous word. The core technical achievement of the project is the integration of three distinct AI decision-making strategies based on difficulty levels: • Easy Mode (Uninformed Search): AI selects words randomly from a common word dictionary. • Medium Mode (Heuristic Search): AI prefers longer words (4-5 letters) to increase scoring opportunities. • Hard Mode (Minimax-like / Greedy Search): AI strategically selects words ending with rare letters (x, z, q, j, v) to trap the player. The project implements a timer system, scoring mechanism with bonus points for long words, sound effects, cartoon characters, and a responsive user interface. The AI successfully provides challenging gameplay while remaining beatable, creating an engaging experience for players of all skill levels. Testing confirms that the AI makes decisions in under 0.1 seconds across all difficulty levels. 2 Introduction 2.1 Overview of the Game Word Chain Game is a turn-based game where a player competes against an AI opponent. The AI starts by selecting a random word from a common word dictionary. The player must then enter a word that starts with the last letter of the AI’s word. The AI responds similarly, creating a chain of words. The game continues until either player cannot think of a valid word or the time runs out. The game features: • Three difficulty levels (Easy, Medium, Hard) • Timer system (per move and total game time) • Scoring system with bonuses for long words • Sound effects with on/off toggle • Cartoon characters for engagement • Rules page explaining gameplay 4\n\nAI Project Report Word Chain Game 2.2 Purpose of the Project The primary motivation behind this project is to demonstrate the practical application of Search Algorithms in an interactive gaming environment. While word chain games are typically played casually, this project treats the game as a state-space search problem where the AI must evaluate possible moves and select optimal ones based on difficultyspecific strategies. The purpose is to explore how an AI agent can: • Make decisions using different search strategies • Adapt its behavior based on difficulty levels • Provide challenging yet beatable gameplay • Maintain real-time responsiveness 2.3 Objectives The development and analysis of the project were guided by the following key objectives: 1. Build an AI-Based Game Environment: Develop a robust, stable, and responsive web application using Python Flask that accurately manages game state, validates moves, and enforces game rules. 2. Implement Decision-Making Algorithms: Integrate three distinct AI strategies: • Uninformed Search (Random) for Easy mode • Heuristic Search (Length-based) for Medium mode • Minimax-like / Greedy Search (Rare letters) for Hard mode 3. Create Engaging User Experience: Design a responsive interface with animations, sound effects, cartoon characters, and real-time feedback. 4. Evaluate Performance Metrics: Establish a quantitative framework to assess AI response time, decision quality, and player engagement across difficulty levels. 3 Game Description & Design 3.1 Game Rules The objective of the game is to create the longest possible chain of words following the word chain rule. Core Mechanics: • Each word must start with the last letter of the previous word • No word can be repeated during a single game • Words must exist in the dictionary • Time limits apply per move and total game time 5\n\nAI Project Report Word Chain Game Player vs AI Interaction: • AI always starts the game with a random word • Player enters a word starting with AI’s last letter • AI responds with another word • Game continues until time runs out or no valid words remain Winning Conditions: • Player wins by having a higher score when time expires • Player wins if AI has no valid words to play • AI wins if player has no valid words to play • AI wins if player runs out of time Losing Conditions: • Time Out: If the player fails to submit a word within the per-move time limit, AI receives +20 points and the player loses the turn • No Valid Words: If the player cannot think of any word starting with the required letter, the player loses immediately • Invalid Word: Entering a word not in the dictionary, a repeated word, or a word with wrong starting letter results in a loss of turn and AI gets an opportunity • Total Game Time Expiry: If the total game time (2-3 minutes depending on difficulty) reaches zero, the player with lower score loses • Violation of Word Length: In Medium mode (4-5 letters) or Hard mode (67 letters), entering a word with incorrect length causes immediate rejection and counts as an invalid move Time Limits per Difficulty: Difficulty Per Move Time Total Game Time Easy 15 seconds 2 minutes (120 sec) Medium 20 seconds 2.5 minutes (150 sec) Hard 25 seconds 3 minutes (180 sec) Table 1: Time Limits by Difficulty Word Length Requirements per Difficulty: Difficulty Minimum Length Maximum Length Easy 2 letters No maximum Medium 4 letters 5 letters Hard 6 letters 7 letters Table 2: Word Length Requirements 6\n\nAI Project Report Word Chain Game Summary of Losing Conditions: Condition Consequence Affected Player Time Out (per move) AI receives +20 points Player loses turn No valid words available Immediate loss Player or AI Word not in dictionary Move rejected, turn lost Player Wrong starting letter Move rejected, turn lost Player Repeated word Move rejected, turn lost Player Total game time expiry Lower score loses Player or AI Length violation (Medium/Hard) Move rejected Player Table 3: Summary of Losing Conditions 3.2 Game Environment The game environment is a web-based interface designed with a focus on clear state represent