e state is represented by: • Set of used words • Current last letter • Player and AI scores • Remaining move time • Remaining total game time 5 System Architecture The architecture of the system follows a modular design, ensuring a clear separation between the user interface, the game logic, and the artificial intelligence module. 5.1 Block Diagram Description The system operates in a cyclical feedback loop: 1. User Input triggers a state change in the Game Engine 2. Game Engine validates the move and updates game state 3. AI Module generates response based on difficulty 4. Output Display renders the updated state for the user 5.2 Component Breakdown Component Layer Function User Input Presentation Captures mouse clicks and keyboard events via JavaScript Game Engine Processing Maintains game state, enforces rules, validates moves AI Module Intelligence Generates AI responses using difficulty-specific algorithms Output Display Presentation Renders game state, scores, timers, and animations Dictionaries Data Stores common words (AI) and full dictionary (validation) Table 6: System Components 15\n\nAI Project Report Word Chain Game 5.3 Architecture Diagram Figure 8: System Architecture Block Diagram 6 Simulation of Game & AI Behavior 6.1 Game Play Simulation The following table tracks a sequence of moves from the start of a game, showcasing the turn-based interaction between Player and AI. Turn Player Word Last Letter Player Score AI Score 1 AI apple e 0 10 2 Player elephant t 20 10 3 AI tiger r 20 30 4 Player rabbit t 40 30 5 AI table e 40 50 6 Player egg g 55 50 7 AI goat t 55 70 8 Player tree e 75 70 9 AI eagle e 75 90 Table 7: Game Play Simulation Trace 16\n\nAI Project Report Word Chain Game Figure 9: Easy Mode Gameplay Figure 10: Medium Mode Gameplay Figure 11: Hard Mode Gameplay Figure 12: Simulation Screenshots for Easy, Medium, and Hard Modes 17\n\nAI Project Report Word Chain Game 6.2 AI Decision Simulation Scenario 1: Easy Mode Parameter Value Last Letter ’e